    "ledger_voiced": "From my book. The sitting ran as I ran it: the spirit writing: her knee against the leaf; the spirit trumpet: the wedge of a boot; the scent of violets: a stuffed glove; the guttering of the lamp: the window cord; the touch: a trimmed wick; the raps: a changed slate. The table's tilt I did not produce, and did not care for.\n\nAs to the evening's business: the account Zane Swain swore to was an invention, for those hands were out of the dark and about their own work. Captain Wat Frew was past any sitting's reach before the lamps were lit.\n\nThe dead say what it profits me they say; on this occasion they profited Zane Swain more.",
